SunOS client libraries (SP and MP): the SunOS block links the client with
-lX11 -lXext -liconv, left from the SDL 1.2 days. iconv is in libc on
illumos and Solaris 11 (there is no libiconv, so the link fails), and the
client calls no X11 function itself (SDL2 does). Link $(SDL_LIBS) -lm, as the
other Unix platforms do.

Upstream: not submitted yet; no issue or pull request about it at
https://github.com/iortcw/iortcw (checked 2026-11-10).

--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/Makefile.orig
+++ iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/Makefile
@@ -1031,7 +1031,7 @@
 
   BOTCFLAGS=-O0
 
-  CLIENT_LIBS +=$(SDL_LIBS) -lX11 -lXext -liconv -lm
+  CLIENT_LIBS +=$(SDL_LIBS) -lm
   RENDERER_LIBS = $(SDL_LIBS)
 
 else # ifeq sunos
--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/MP/Makefile.orig
+++ iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/MP/Makefile
@@ -1042,7 +1042,7 @@
 
   BOTCFLAGS=-O0
 
-  CLIENT_LIBS +=$(SDL_LIBS) -lX11 -lXext -liconv -lm
+  CLIENT_LIBS +=$(SDL_LIBS) -lm
   RENDERER_LIBS = $(SDL_LIBS)
 
 else # ifeq sunos
